NUGpq3xu8JCTYw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:MinorityInterestInLimitedPartnerships" scale="6" id="Narr_PF5HOp_6SkWBzUjPhEcGcg">10.11</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively. The reduction in carrying value during the Current Year reflects the Current Year loss detailed above, plus the settlement of the contingent contractual obligation related to IM Topco as described in Note 9, as a result of which the previously recorded liability was de-recognized by reducing the value of the investment. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Investment in Other Unconsolidated Affiliate</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">In December 2023, the Company contributed $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_zZYrRzoJIUyD7mfk1ybfHg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaymentsToAcquireEquityMethodInvestments" scale="6" id="Narr_mB5WsTxgR06cRGk-MzA7KQ">0.15</ix:nonFraction> million of cash to a privately-held corporation (the &#8220;Affiliate&#8221;) in exchange for a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2023_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_h9ueFU4ovEKHCB9zHOd-ag" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:MinorityInterestOwnershipPercentageByParent" scale="-2" id="Narr_6wIQBWF8mUqsc727qdSv_w">30</ix:nonFraction>% equity ownership interest in the Affiliate. During the Prior Year, the Company accounted for its interest in the operations of the Affiliate as a component of other operating costs and expenses (income) under the equity method of accounting. The Company&#8217;s proportional share of the operating results of Affiliate for the Prior Year was a loss of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_X3VquFmxKUmAD0lgBM_GHg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeLossFromContinuingOperationsIncludingPortionAttributableToNoncontrollingInterest" sign="-" scale="6" id="Narr_IAs4q0VCxEefP8m9d8Xs0A">0.15</ix:nonFraction> million. Also during the Prior Year, the Company&#8217;s proportional ownership interest in the Affiliate was reduced from <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_c-AymCbjKEyyheLZkeC33g" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:MinorityInterestOwnershipPercentageByParent" scale="-2" id="Narr_n08pTGk6Ck29cFqXPdE9kw">30</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_BRoxKmxmkUKF9hDXMa0A6w" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:MinorityInterestOwnershipPercentageByParent" scale="-2" id="Narr_T0KOc0hQp0qP4SSEeZHhWw">19</ix:nonFraction>% as the result of dilution arising from other parties making investments in the Affiliate; however, by that point, the carrying value of the Company&#8217;s investment in the Affiliate had already been reduced to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_8053UjcMrUOsW4gyNKOkWw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:EquityMethodInvestments" scale="0" id="Narr_II-QebqKqUWK68q0SLzqTA">zero</ix:nonFraction>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">Effective January 2025, the Company no longer applies the equity method of accounting to its investment in the Affiliate. Instead, the Company currently accounts for its investment in the Affiliate in accordance with ASC 321-10-35-2: at adjusted cost, less impairment, plus or minus observable price changes of an identical or similar investment of the same issuer. There were no amounts recognized in the consolidated statement of operations related to the Affiliate for Current Year, and the carrying value of the Company&#8217;s investment in the Affiliate as of both December 31, 2025 and 2024 was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_8053UjcMrUOsW4gyNKOkWw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:EquityMethodInvestments" scale="0" id="Narr_6N1k1hAXH0-GXaPgauLudA"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_OrmeLiveMember_X4XWVTE_TE2dzAxgMZCwxw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:EquityMethodInvestments" scale="0" id="Narr_4BpR5gCukkywLRMlmKqd1w">zero</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>.</p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">67</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 15pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">XCEL BRANDS,&#160;INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes&#160;to Consolidated Financial Statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_lcJq8_Pr2kKcRANj4U1KoQ_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Longaberger Licensing, LLC Variable Interest Entity </span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">Since 2019, Xcel has been party to a limited liability company agreement with a subsidiary of Hilco Global related to Longaberger Licensing, LLC (&#8220;LL&#8221;). Hilco Global is the sole Class A Member of LL, and Xcel is the sole Class B Member of LL (each individually a &#8220;Member&#8221;). Each Member holds a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_us-gaap_VariableInterestEntityPrimaryBeneficiaryMember_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_LongabergerLicensingLLCMember_c-BOrjcyWUC3Ew-u9HBAmg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:VariableInterestEntityOwnershipPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_6JWMNGam30eIE9lGr78_3A">50</ix:nonFraction>% equity ownership interest in LL; however, based on an analysis of the contractual terms and rights contained in the agreements between the Members, the Company has previously determined that under the applicable accounting standards, LL is a variable interest entity and the Company has effective control over LL. Therefore, as the primary beneficiary, the Company has consolidated LL since 2019, and has recognized the assets, liabilities, revenues, and expenses of LL as part of its consolidated financial statements, along with a noncontrolling interest which represents Hilco Global&#8217;s <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_HilcoGlobalMember_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_us-gaap_VariableInterestEntityPrimaryBeneficiaryMember_srt_OwnershipAxis_xelb_LongabergerLicensingLLCMember_fpQMgdRU706ISknMOa1yRQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:VariableInterestEntityOwnershipPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_cf46WIOdY0WZBgV9_TmsZg">50</ix:nonFraction>% ownership share in LL. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Divestiture of the Lori Goldstein Brand</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">On June 21, 2024, the Company (through its wholly owned subsidiary, Gold Licensing, LLC) entered into an asset purchase agreement with Lori Goldstein and Lori Goldstein, Ltd (together the &#8220;LG Parties&#8221;), pursuant to which the Company agreed to sell, and the LG Parties agreed to purchase, substantially all of the assets of the Lori Goldstein Brand, including the &#8220;LOGO by Lori Goldstein&#8221; trademark and other intellectual property rights relating thereto. Also in conjunction with this transaction, key license agreements related to the Lori Goldstein Brand were assigned to and assumed by the LG Parties. This divestiture transaction closed on June 30, 2024.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">As consideration for the sale of these assets, the parties agreed to the following:</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The LG Parties waived their rights with respect to certain contingent consideration amounts that had been previously earned by the LG Parties (under the terms of the April 1, 2021 purchase of the assets by Xcel), and terminated their rights to any future earn-out payments.</span></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 36pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-left:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The Company retained the right to all royalties and fee income for net sales from licensees related to the Lori Goldstein Brand through the closing date.</span></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"><span style="margin-left:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The Company&#8217;s May 2, 2024 termination of the employment agreement and consulting agreement with the LG Parties was withdrawn. The Company paid the LG Parties a combined total of </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_2wmNgeBVDkKzKKwoXL1UHw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AdministrativeFeesExpense" scale="0" id="Narr_GV9t3zUqqU6yKSqF3cJdZg">25,000</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> as compensation for services rendered under the employment agreement and consulting agreement through June 30, 2024, and also reimbursed Ms. Goldstein for expenses incurred in the course of fulfilling her duties under the employment agreement through June 30, 2024.</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The Company and the LG Parties entered into a mutual general release and waiver of outstanding legal disputes. &#160;</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:12pt;"></div><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The total consideration received by the Company for this divestiture transaction was approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_2wmNgeBVDkKzKKwoXL1UHw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromDivestitureOfBusinesses" scale="6" id="Narr_nShT_bFzE0a3CsClk9lDDA">6.08</ix:nonFraction> million, comprised of (i) the waiver of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_2wmNgeBVDkKzKKwoXL1UHw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AssetAcquisitionEarnOutPayments" scale="6" id="Narr_UGEmaC4VqkOxvPzmrId6kg">1.03</ix:nonFraction> million of accrued earn-out payments earned by the LG Parties through June 30, 2024, plus (ii) the release of the remaining balance of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_7gpcOU1RZE2eDU8E9eolkQ" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AssetAcquisitionContingentConsiderationLiability" scale="6" id="Narr_4q6cib3RQUOQq8HxOxa_vA">5.05</ix:nonFraction> million of contingent obligations recorded on the Company&#8217;s balance sheet. The remaining unamortized net book value of the Lori Goldstein intangible assets immediately prior to the sale was approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_2wmNgeBVDkKzKKwoXL1UHw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromSaleOfIntangibleAssets" scale="6" id="Narr_AECtra6RBkSAzuJsjdmguQ">1.93</ix:nonFraction> million, and the Company also incurred approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_2wmNgeBVDkKzKKwoXL1UHw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LegalFees" scale="6" id="Narr_JgEFsQ5wzkqNnK6GnruSRg">0.35</ix:nonFraction> million of legal fees in connection with this transaction. Accordingly, the Company recorded a net non-cash gain on the divestiture of the Lori Goldstein Brand of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_2wmNgeBVDkKzKKwoXL1UHw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:GainLossOnDispositionOfAssets1" scale="6" id="Narr_POiVmpHvi0aeC1MMXhRIMQ">3.80</ix:nonFraction> million for the year ended December 31, 2024.</p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:ce