urrent terms are $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_hin6VKrnPE6XXNbLFvgCOA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ContractualObligation" scale="6" id="Narr_Dim9HTkk40CL-u8_hwQd8Q">2.20</ix:nonFraction> million, of which $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_hin6VKrnPE6XXNbLFvgCOA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ContractualObligationDueInNextTwelveMonths" scale="6" id="Narr_MGPWtoQTR0qSOtiX6OCKGQ">2.01</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_hin6VKrnPE6XXNbLFvgCOA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ContractualObligationDueInSecondYear" scale="6" id="Narr_2H6FNdBcdESmm5FGw3hIHA">0.18</ix:nonFraction> million will be paid during the years ending December 31, 2026 and 2027, respectively. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In addition, the Company&#8217;s employment contracts with certain executives contain performance-based bonus provisions, which include bonuses based on the Company achieving revenues in excess of established targets and/or on operating results.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Certain of the employment agreements contain severance and/or change in control provisions. Aggregate potential severance compensation amounted to approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_xLDaje6a3EqUILcqWnocGA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SeveranceCosts1" scale="6" id="Narr_zldSwdostEelXJrN0kOYzw">2.71</ix:nonFraction> million as of December&#160;31, 2025. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Contingent Obligation &#8211; Lori Goldstein Earn-Out</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In connection with the April 1, 2021 purchase of the Lori Goldstein trademarks, the Company had agreed to pay the seller additional cash consideration (the &#8220;Lori Goldstein Earn-Out&#8221;) of up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2021_To_4_1_2021_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_FRrTeTfUuEa7Yp-z3bZI7g" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AssetAcquisitionsContingentConsiderationAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_aVF-02qy40Od7EKAtb3EuQ">12.5</ix:nonFraction> million, based on royalties earned during the <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_cVtxRBPNXU65LvQ3yIHw7A;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">six</span></span> calendar year period commencing in 2021. The Lori Goldstein Earn-Out was initially recorded as a liability of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2021_To_4_1_2021_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_FRrTeTfUuEa7Yp-z3bZI7g" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AssetAcquisitionContingentObligation" scale="6" id="Narr_swr2WMkCyEai3uSkEQyOsQ">6.6</ix:nonFraction> million, based on the difference between the fair value of the acquired assets of the Lori Goldstein brand and the total consideration paid, in accordance with the guidance in ASC Subtopic 805-50. Through January 1, 2024, the Company paid $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_5_1_2021_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_RFOe9zomAUGuPwEm43t0nw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:PaymentsOfContingentConsideration" scale="6" id="Narr__YG4I0axYkOHdPU7oDLgog">0.2</ix:nonFraction> million to the seller, and as of January 1, 2024, the remaining balance of the contingent obligation was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_1_1_2024_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_5qDCr2XRokaHSDAS9CUORg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AssetAcquisitionContingentConsiderationLiability" scale="6" id="Narr_Ziotu6KwzUOz5br4Yd41cw">6.4</ix:nonFraction> million, of which approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_1_1_2024_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_5qDCr2XRokaHSDAS9CUORg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AssetAcquisitionContingentConsiderationLiabilityCurrent" scale="6" id="Narr_0MiAM40zMUm-75bUYbxkUg">1.03</ix:nonFraction> million had been earned and was payable to the seller. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During the year ended December 31, 2024, the Company paid approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_Nb_Rj860XE6uc7ts5RCnpA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:PaymentsOfContingentConsideration" scale="6" id="Narr_Tqre-fro9kqpoDckEFaSRw">0.3</ix:nonFraction> million of the $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_Nb_Rj860XE6uc7ts5RCnpA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AssetAcquisitionAdditionalConsiderationPayableToSeller" scale="6" id="Narr_2vJZVqmDM0KzIaX4yvnO-g">1.0</ix:nonFraction> million earned to the seller. However, as a result of the June 30, 2024 divestiture of the Lori Goldstein brand (as described in Note 3), the seller waived their rights with respect to the Lori Goldstein Earn-Out amounts that had been previously earned and had not yet been paid, and terminated their rights to any future payments under the Lori Goldstein Earn-Out. As a result, the Company de-recognized approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_6_30_2024_To_6_30_2024_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_vJA2m7PQAU20KhnhkHIvNw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AssetAcquisitionEarnOutPayments" scale="6" id="Narr_Ci_j98eGxEihYwhixsUCzg">1.03</ix:nonFraction> million of accrued Lori Goldstein Earn-Out payments and the remaining balance of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2024_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_vWT8pZ6Mdke5ua3fKjrQ2Q" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AssetAcquisitionContingentConsiderationLiabilityDerecognized" scale="6" id="Narr_0grhWYguKkSZqn-NBB_cFA">5.05</ix:nonFraction> million of contingent obligations recorded on the Company&#8217;s balance sheet. As of December 31, 2024, there were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_AssetAcquisitionAxis_xelb_LoriGoldsteinBrandMember_bEOHVTvafEG47fp2M-7K9A" decimals="-4" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:AssetAcquisitionContingentConsiderationLiability" scale="6" id="Narr_03Sq_O0Hh0-qsJxje_iiQQ">no</ix:nonFraction> liability amounts remaining on the Company&#8217;s consolidated balance sheet related to the Lori Goldstein Earn-Out.</p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">85</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 15pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">XCEL BRANDS,&#160;INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes&#160;to Consolidated Financial Statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_jK7kU9tTo0-kkhDu2RJWCw_cont3"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Contingent Obligation &#8211; Isaac Mizrahi Transaction</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In connection with the May 31, 2022 transaction related to the sale of a majority interest in the Isaac Mizrahi Brand, the Company agreed with WHP that, in the event that IM Topco receives less than $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2022_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_DisposalGroupClassificationAxis_us-gaap_DisposalGroupDisposedOfBySaleNotDiscontinuedOperationsMember_us-gaap_OtherCommitmentsAxis_xelb_IsaacMizrahiSaleTransactionWithImTopcoMember_vTP4s8ZpAkS8U6OIa2SV_Q" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RoyaltyGuaranteesCommitmentsAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_RVr5RPAi1k2pBc06VP_gSQ">13.3</ix:nonFraction> million in aggregate royalties for any <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_oEke_C_eCkSlEzHr8RCAlw" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2022_us-gaap_DisposalGroupClassificationAxis_us-gaap_DisposalGroupDisposedOfBySaleNotDiscontinuedOperationsMember_us-gaap_OtherCommitmentsAxis_xelb_IsaacMizrahiSaleTransactionWithImTopcoMember_T1HHIt5r_k2zbRpXd51m5g" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="xelb:NumberOfConsecutiveQuartersForRoyaltyPayableTerm" scale="0" id="Narr_hwObNaIHnEGw_oVBl4FyVA">four</ix:nonFraction> consecutive calendar quarters over a <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_5_31_2022_To_5_31_2022_us-gaap_DisposalGroupClassificationAxis_us-gaap_DisposalGroupDisposedOfBySaleNotDiscontinuedOperationsMember_us-gaap_OtherCommitmentsAxis_xelb_IsaacMizrahiSaleTransactionWithImTopcoMember_ioBI3flmpUCCmPWOErJz_w" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="xelb:RoyaltyPayableTerm" id="Narr_mWxcSOvxSUCXnpj_v870YA">three-year</ix:nonNumeric> period ending on May 31, 2025, WHP would be entitled to receive from Xcel up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_5_31_2022_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_DisposalGroupClassificationAxis_us-gaap_DisposalGroupDisposedOfBySaleNotDiscontinuedOperationsMember_us-gaap_OtherCommitmentsAxis_xelb_IsaacMizrahiSaleTransactionWithImTopcoMember_vTP4s8ZpAkS8U6OIa2SV_Q" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AdjustmentToPurchasePricePayable" scale="6" id="Narr_eh3N6uKmAE21FdOeo_gqow">16</ix:nonFraction> million, less all amounts of net cash flow distributed to WHP on an accumulated basis, as an adjustment to the purchase price previously paid by WHP. Such amount would be payable by the Company in either cash or equity interests in IM Topco held by the Company. In November 2023, this agreement was amended such that the purchase price adjustment provision was waived until the measurement period ending March 31, 2024.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On April 12, 2024, this agreement was further amended such that the purchase price adjustment provision within the membership purchase agreement was waived until the measurement period ending September 30, 2025. This amendment also provided that if (i) IM Topco royalties are less than $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_4_12_2024_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xelb_TwelveMonthPeriodEndingMarch312025Member_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_dbha3Wz8u0-numpLBJ0S5Q" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RoyaltyGuaranteesCommitmentsAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_B9kgfQtkQUO6AfWzLiMuLQ">13.5</ix:nonFraction> million for the twelve-month period ending March 31, 2025 or (ii) IM Topco royalties are less than $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_4_12_2024_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xelb_YearEndingDecember312025Member_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_DYJJ3h5_TEelbSAzb9PIdA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RoyaltyGuaranteesCommitmentsAmount" scale="6" id="Narr__LLl82zUo02tViXj89bx-g">18.0</ix:nonFraction> million for the year ending December 31, 2025 or (iii) Xcel fails to make certain payments to IM Topco under the terms of the license agreement between Xcel and IM Topco (see Note 11) on or before January 30, 2025, then Xcel shall transfer equity interests in IM Topco to WHP equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="Duration_4_12_2024_To_4_12_2024_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xelb_IfRoyaltiesReceivableLessThanSpecifiedAmountMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_cEtxJdNb2kaWKmplAYPgeQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:OwnershipInterestTransferable" scale="-2" id="Narr_BSeG4daXc0aZMMianXAM3g">12.5</ix:nonFraction>% of the total outstanding equity interests of IM Topco, such that Xcel&#8217;s ownership interest in IM Topco would decrease from <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="As_Of_4_12_2024_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_XcelBrandsMember_srt_ScheduleOfEquityMethodInvestmentEquityMethodInvesteeNameAxis_xelb_IMTopcoLLCMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_2kBDm87vlk6x60r86kthJA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EquityMethodInvestmentOwnershipPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_HnviLVVPKUKKODKKVjtkNQ">30</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="As_Of_4_12_2024_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_XcelBrandsMember_srt_ScheduleOfEquityMethodInvestmentEquityMethodInvesteeNameAxis_xelb_IMTopcoLLCMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xelb_IfRoyaltiesReceivableLessThanSpecifiedAmountMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_Q5hpipYwLUiCy8T1qI2pfA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EquityMethodInvestmentOwnershipPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_sC08ew3I_kClxz9ErzCktQ">17.5</ix:nonFraction>%, and WHP&#8217;s ownership interest in IM Topco would increase from <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="As_Of_4_12_2024_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_ImWhpLlcMember_srt_ScheduleOfEquityMethodInvestmentEquityMethodInvesteeNameAxis_xelb_IMTopcoLLCMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_e4fXeQ8K2keLHhHvoOzBMA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EquityMethodInvestmentOwnershipPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_-m_9rmoBek-4G2TPGIXLIQ">70</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_oi117mk2RU2JajuxvTP2NA" contextRef="As_Of_4_12_2024_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_ImWhpLlcMember_srt_ScheduleOfEquityMethodInvestmentEquityMethodInvesteeNameAxis_xelb_IMTopcoLLCMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xelb_IfRoyaltiesReceivableLessThanSpecifiedAmountMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_Ykl2_eeUzUOYN_MK89tZ0w" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EquityMethodInvestmentOwnershipPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_-Bd7kvBmqEuWH1AsIwMMSw">82.5</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During the Prior Year, management concluded that, based on current trends in and projections of IM Topco&#8217;s royalty revenues as well as the Company&#8217;s decision to not make the remaining royalty payments to IM Topco, it was virtually certain that the Company would be required to make such transfer of equity interests to WHP in 2025. As such, the Company estimated and recorded a contingent obligation of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_ImWhpLlcMember_srt_ScheduleOfEquityMethodInvestmentEquityMethodInvesteeNameAxis_xelb_IMTopcoLLCMember_nRL8xHv7JkqmwV6M3clojA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AssetAcquisitionContingentConsiderationLiabilityCurrent" scale="6" id="Narr_sXzuptY2V0GcGuzZ4dnKbA">4.21</ix:nonFraction> million in the accompanying consolidated balance sheets, and recognized a corresponding non-cash charge in the consolidated statements of operations for the Prior Year. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During the Current Year, the Company adjusted the carrying value of the contingent obligation to its estimated fair value of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_4_15_2025_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_ImWhpLlcMember_srt_ScheduleOfEquityMethodInvestmentEquityMethodInvesteeNameAxis_xelb_IMTopcoLLCMember_mDeghcgK_ECp6pzvP1lJUg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AssetAcquisitionContingentConsiderationFairValue" scale="6" id="Narr_1qdggYqfOUqegGm8KZcSOQ">3.97</ix:nonFraction> million, and recognized a $(<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_4_15_2025_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xelb_ImWhpLlcMember_srt_ScheduleOfEquityMethodInvestmentEquityMethodInvesteeNameAxis_xelb_IMTopcoLLCMember_5FgmJXWR-US4vNhWG55bkA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:GainLossOnRemeasurementOfContingentConsiderationForAssetAcquisition" sign="-" scale="6" id="Narr_A-_X1oghO0CAwUXd1o1Tgg">0.24</ix:nonFraction>) million credit in the consolidated statements of operations. On and effective April 15, 2025, such equity interests were transferred to WHP in full satisfaction and settlement of this contractual obligation, and the previously recorded liability was de-recognized by reducing the value of the asset for the investment in IM Topco.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Legal Proceedings</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">From time to time, the Company becomes involved in legal claims and litigation in the ordinary course of business. The Company routinely assesses all its litigation and threatened litigation as to the probability of ultimately incurring a liability and records its best estimate of the ultimate loss in situations where it assesses the likelihood of loss as probable. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">In the opinion o