ximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_us-gaap_DomesticCountryMember_UsWDaYmjTkGCXbwC8Oa5Kw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" scale="6" id="Narr_pCegg1ggEUCPTcwX5fKm-w">59.1</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_us-gaap_DomesticCountryMember_NYyIs9PzZ0mwpT8EjW7Byw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" scale="6" id="Narr_bKSmNXQhykaWxZYBbDUSBw">44.4</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively, of federal net operating loss carryforwards ("NOLs") available to offset future taxable income. The federal NOL as of December&#160;31, 2017 of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2017_zTZWTHtDE0SHRtZhK_rBgA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" scale="6" id="Narr_NdPxtC9y9kegDtBlT4S1QQ">0.3</ix:nonFraction> million has an expiration period through 2037. The federal NOLs generated during tax&#160;years beginning after December&#160;31, 2017 of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_TaxPeriodAxis_xelb_IndefiniteLivedMember_p7wHPjBSY0S-LLfc-zXPJA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" scale="6" id="Narr_6gE-2mnvT0WokZV_99RGwA">58.8</ix:nonFraction> million have an indefinite life and do not expire. The Company has approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_us-gaap_StateAndLocalJurisdictionMember_EGCzN_5E4Ui9TJamf3K-Fw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" scale="6" id="Narr_GsdukwJjw0CgbsT4s5tFlA">72.7</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_us-gaap_StateAndLocalJurisdictionMember_Fd5UV5_fakmiW1UYqn98CA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OperatingLossCarryforwards" scale="6" id="Narr_CQPEA1f5iU-zczHn1eBv3g">54.1</ix:nonFraction> million of state NOLs as of December 31, 2025 and December 31, 2024, respectively. The state NOLs expire at various times between 2035 and 2045. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">As of December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024, management does not believe the Company has any material uncertain tax positions that would require it to measure and reflect the potential lack of sustainability of a position on audit in its consolidated financial statements. The Company will continue to evaluate its uncertain tax positions in future periods to determine if measurement and recognition in its consolidated financial statements is necessary. The Company does not believe there will be any material changes in its unrecognized tax positions over the next&#160;year.</p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_xLDaje6a3EqUILcqWnocGA" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionsDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_g6oe5Pl6JUK-vqvV4QgtsQ" continuedAt="Tb_g6oe5Pl6JUK-vqvV4QgtsQ_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">11. &#160;&#160;Related Party Transactions</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">IM Topco, LLC</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As described in Note 3, the Company held a noncontrolling interest in IM Topco through October 1, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;">Services Agreement</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The Company was party to a services agreement with IM Topco that had been originally effective May 31 2022 and subsequently amended from time to time, pursuant to which the Company agreed to provide certain design and support services (including assistance with the operations of the interactive television business and related talent support) to IM </p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">88</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 15pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">XCEL BRANDS,&#160;INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes&#160;to Consolidated Financial Statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_g6oe5Pl6JUK-vqvV4QgtsQ_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_g6oe5Pl6JUK-vqvV4QgtsQ_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Topco in exchange for a service fee. In April 2024, the services agreement was amended to set the service fees at $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="As_Of_4_30_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_ImTopcoMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_AmendedServicesAgreementMember_GA2a03IQl02flmmAhyLLKQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherReceivables" scale="0" id="Narr_BU-7bQTU_kybTdiLzuxR7w">150,000</ix:nonFraction> per year.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In accordance with the terms of this services agreement, the Company recognized service fee income of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_ImTopcoMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_ServicesAgreementMember_qamIORRbKUSSFJc2RbiCVA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Revenues" scale="0" id="Narr_Q7tgILUkLE2WwoQsmOu8Sw">112,500</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_ImTopcoMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_ServicesAgreementMember_x9bARqfMwkmzQiVxeRHpaQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Revenues" scale="0" id="Narr_vprvwEb2i0-_0x5I23c6dw">150,000</ix:nonFraction> for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;">License Agreement</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company was previously party to a license agreement with IM Topco, pursuant to which IM Topco granted the Company a license to use certain Isaac Mizrahi trademarks related to women&#8217;s sportswear products in exchange for the payment of royalties to IM Topco. This license agreement was later terminated in favor of a new similar license agreement between IM Topco and an unrelated third party; however, as part of such termination, Xcel had provided a guarantee to IM Topco for the payment of any difference between (i) the royalties received by IM Topco under the new agreement and (ii) the amount of royalties that IM Topco would have received under the original license agreement with Xcel. For both the Current Year and Prior Year, royalties received by IM Topco from the third-party agreement were expected to exceed the guaranteed royalties that IM Topco would have received under the original license agreement with Xcel, and thus no royalty expense for any shortfall was recognized for either such period.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Additionally, pursuant to the terms of a 2023 amendment to the May 2022 membership purchase agreement, Xcel had agreed to make additional royalty payments to IM Topco totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_ImTopcoMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_LicenseAgreementMember_hFoWQ01MLke8pGxy3ujjFQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:NoncontrollingInterestIncreaseFromSubsidiaryEquityIssuance" scale="0" id="Narr_Uqh4zr3kmkSTjRXmQ17Siw">450,000</ix:nonFraction>, of which $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_ImTopcoMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_LicenseAgreementMember_hFoWQ01MLke8pGxy3ujjFQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaymentsForRoyalties" scale="0" id="Narr_QTvrynp-qkKuvbsVgdzz9Q">75,000</ix:nonFraction> was paid during the year ended December 31, 2023, and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_ImTopcoMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_LicenseAgreementMember_vqR3mra7SEWvb-DCD6FPgA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaymentsForRoyalties" scale="0" id="Narr_L-RDXJ8z1kCiNo_M4pgNOw">237,500</ix:nonFraction> was paid during the year ended December 31, 2024. <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_y9EXRe8KL0q_GXXbhqC2Yg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_ImTopcoMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_xelb_LicenseAgreementMember_HtJDKkADzUe8RR29pvmiEg" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:PaymentsForRoyalties" scale="0" id="Narr_dZ64gwR3KkuFX8l6mIw9BQ">No</ix:nonFraction> payments of these additional royalties were made during the year ended December 31, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Effective September 26, 2025, pursuant to the terms of a settlement agreement entered into with IM Topco and WHP (see Note 3 for additional details), the Company was released from any current or future liability related to the aforementioned guarantee to IM Topco and the aforementioned additional royalty payments.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Equity Offerings</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;">August 2025 Public Offering and Private Placement Transactions</i> &#8211; In connection with the public offering which closed on August 4, 2025 (see Note 7 for additional details), Robert W. D&#8217;Loren, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of the Company, and Mark DiSanto, a director of the Company, purchased <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_prl09U-R0E2XnR3uIo925w" contextRef="As_Of_8_4_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_xelb_PublicOfferingMember_-2e85MAKIEe5SNJOUHkSKw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_67VbVg0fHkirECEFhUtzKg">124,200</ix:nonFraction> and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_prl09U-R0E2XnR3uIo925w" contextRef="As_Of_8_4_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_xelb_PublicOfferingMember_7vjKAXChc0mKyY3uobMERw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_7Pgr6UOkeEayTG5VdC4MHQ">91,800</ix:nonFraction> shares of common stock, respectively, at $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_JH3LV_Tylk-VFDaz510hgA" contextRef="As_Of_8_4_2025_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_xelb_PublicOfferingMember_8eT2yN6OaEiRuIoa_xQk3g" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharesIssuedPricePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_HbBEJqycX0Osg0jJAdJx9Q">1.10</ix:nonFraction> per share, the same price at which the shares were sold to other purchasers in the public offering. Also, in connection with this public offering, on August 1, 2025, the Company entered into subscription agreements with each of Mr. D&#8217;Loren and Mr. DiSanto to purchase <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_prl09U-R0E2XnR3uIo925w" contextRef="As_Of_8_1_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_ChiefExecutiveOfficerMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_PrivatePlacementMember_WT33ESHe_E22_ah6qlQEiw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_AaNuQ16QKE-cD54nGUEtzw">82,159</ix:nonFraction> and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_prl09U-R0E2XnR3uIo925w" contextRef="As_Of_8_1_2025_srt_TitleOfIndividualAxis_srt_DirectorMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_PrivatePlacementMember_AlYczB2ARkeQbHf6MBoIPg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_VTKOgiy05ECpalXwxBZF4w">60,883</ix:nonFraction> shares of common stock, respectively, at a price of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_JH3LV_Tylk-VFDaz510hgA" contextRef="As_Of_8_1_2025_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_PrivatePlacementMember_9rGe6yrhKku0QUo1h14ttg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharesIssuedPricePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_r_kafk7j-k-Z4Y1u7XoQXQ